# Copilot CLI driver for the agent-teammates scripts. The operations and their contract are the ones in
# ../CONTRACT.md; read that file first. This driver is turn-based: each `copilot -p` run is one turn and the
# process exits when the turn ends, so a teammate is re-tasked by `send` (resume the same --session-id), not by a message.
# `launch` opens no viewer pane (the runs are `-p` turns), so VIEWER in team.env is ignored.
# It has no advisor-probe, so team-preflight prints `ADVISOR n/a (copilot)`.
# The permission flags are guardrails, not a sandbox: every run gets --add-dir <team-dir>, and a writer also gets
# --add-dir for the agent-teammates scripts dir and for PREFLIGHT_SCRIPTS and TEAM_SCRIPTS from team.env. A read-only
# teammate can write any path through `git log/diff --output=`, and writers' denies match only the literal prefixes.
# See ../../../references/harness-copilot.md (Security caveats) before a run.
LIVE_MESSAGING=0
SEND=script
# `send` waits up to COPILOT_SEND_WAIT seconds (default 60) for the session's previous turn to exit before it refuses,
# so a re-task can block that long.
#
# Per-session state: <team-dir>/copilot-<session-id> holds name, workdir, model, effort, ro, pid, pgid, started, stopped and resumed as
# key=value lines. <team-dir>/copilot-<session-id>.out and .err hold the last run's stdout and stderr.
# Skills are invoked as /<name>.
SKILL_PREFIX=/
